# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
config RUST_PID
	bool "Rust PID management"
	depends on RUST
	default y
	help
	  Build the PID allocator, namespace/task lookup and linkage, pidfd
	  syscall bodies and PID namespace sysctl policy from kernel/pid.rs
	  in the original kernel/pid.o slot. Configured kernel types come
	  from bindgen; macro, locking, refcount and RCU primitives and native
	  ABI metadata use pid_helpers.o. All initial PID and namespace
	  data, flexible-array storage and static relocations remain in Rust.
	  PID_NS, SYSCTL, USER_NS and MULTIUSER retain their original branches.
	  Turning this option off selects the unchanged original C provider.
